---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../../../components/Section.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import DocTable from '../../../components/DocTable.astro';
import DocNote from '../../../components/DocNote.astro';
import { pluginDocs } from '../../../data/site';
import captureSource from '../../../examples/output-capture.ts?raw';

const index = pluginDocs.findIndex((doc) => doc.slug === 'output');
const prev = pluginDocs[index - 1]!;
const next = pluginDocs[index + 1]!;
---

<Base
  title="Output plugin API — modplayjs"
  description="The OutputPlugin contract: start/stop, the exact playBuffer return and loop semantics, sizing and pacing, with a capture example."
  layout="docs"
>
  <div class="breadcrumbs py-0 font-mono text-[0.64rem] text-base-content/30">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/api" class="hover:text-primary">Library API</a></li>
      <li><a href="/api/plugins" class="hover:text-primary">Plugin authoring</a></li>
      <li class="text-base-content/50">Output</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <header class="mt-3 border-b border-base-300 pb-8">
    <p class="font-mono text-[0.64rem] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-base-content/35">
      Plugin authoring / 04
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Output plugin</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-[0.96rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/65">
      Outputs pull. The core never pushes: an output decides when its sink can take more and calls
      <span class="font-mono text-[0.86rem]">core.playBuffer</span>. That clock is what keeps the song position aligned
      with what the listener hears.
    </p>
  </header>

  <Section index="01" title="The interface" note="started by the app">
    <CodeBlock
      title="OutputPlugin"
      code={`import type { Core } from '@modplayjs/core';

interface OutputPlugin {
  readonly name: string;

  /** Begin output. The host app calls this; the core does not. */
  start(core: Core): void;

  /** Stop output and release the device. */
  stop(): void;
}`}
    />
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[74ch] text-[0.86rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/55">
      Registering an output does not start it. The demo starts the WebAudio output from a click handler (the browser
      gesture requirement); an offline writer starts and drains synchronously.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      title="Register and start"
      code={`import { createPcmOutput } from '@modplayjs/out-pcm';

const output = createPcmOutput();
core.registries.registerOutput(output);
output.start(core);   // after core.startPlayer()`}
    />
  </Section>

  <Section index="02" title="playBuffer, exactly" note="the part that trips people up">
    <CodeBlock
      title="core.playBuffer"
      lang="TypeScript"
      code={`playBuffer(out: Float32Array, size: number, loop = 1): number`}
    />
    <DocTable
      columns={['Return', 'Meaning']}
      rows={[
        ['> 0', 'Number of interleaved floats written. Normally equals size when a whole buffer was available.'],
        ['0', 'The song ended while this buffer was being filled. The audio already written is valid; the rest of the buffer is zero-filled. Stop after this call.'],
        ['- 1', 'The song was already ended when the call started. Nothing was written. This is the definitive end signal.'],
      ]}
    />
    <DocTable
      columns={['loop', 'Behaviour']}
      rows={[
        ['1 (default)', 'Play the module once. The core stops when loop_count reaches 1.'],
        ['n > 0', 'Play up to n loops, then stop.'],
        ['0', 'Ignore the loop count: play forever (the endless path).'],
      ]}
    />
    <DocNote tone="warn">
      <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">0</span> and <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">-1</span> are different
      end signals. Treating <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">0</span> as “nothing was written” drops the final
      partial buffer; treating <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">-1</span> as “keep pulling” spins forever.
    </DocNote>
  </Section>

  <Section index="03" title="Sizing and pacing" note="whole ticks only">
    <ul class="max-w-[74ch] space-y-2 text-[0.88rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/60">
      <li>
        <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">playBuffer</span> copies whole ticks. The buffer must hold at least
        <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">ticksize × 2</span> floats or it cannot make progress; a partial tick is
        carried into the next call, not dropped.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">ticksize</span> changes with BPM. Size for at least four ticks of headroom,
        e.g. <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">new Float32Array(core.ticksize * 2 * 4)</span>.
      </li>
      <li>
        In a real-time sink, pull only when the device buffer is below its high-water mark. The core’s song clock
        advances when audio is pulled, so pulling ahead is what makes a pattern view run ahead of what is audible.
      </li>
      <li>
        Do not call <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">playBuffer</span> from two threads for the same core.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section index="04" title="Example: capture to memory" note="offline">
    <p class="max-w-[74ch] text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/60">
      An offline writer can drain the module synchronously. This keeps the partial tail that
      <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">0</span> reports and stops on <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">-1</span>.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock title="capture.ts" lang="TypeScript" code={captureSource} />
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[74ch] text-[0.86rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/55">
      <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">@modplayjs/out-pcm</span> is the fuller version: tick-accurate offline
      render plus a 16-bit stereo RIFF/WAVE encoder.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section index="05" title="Real-time and the browser" note="pull when the sink is hungry">
    <p class="max-w-[74ch] text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/60">
      A device output owns a ring or a FIFO. Pull when its fill drops below the high-water mark, write what the device
      can take, and let the device clock do the pacing. Never busy-loop <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">playBuffer</span>
      on the main thread in a real-time app; the render-ahead will run away from the audible position.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[74ch] text-[0.9rem] leading-relaxed text-base-content/60">
      <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">@modplayjs/out-webaudio</span> implements two transports: a
      SharedArrayBuffer ring when <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">crossOriginIsolated</span>, and a transferable
      copy mode otherwise. Its <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">start(core, workletUrl)</span> takes an extra
      argument, and it adds <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">pause()</span>,
      <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">resume()</span> and <span class="font-mono text-[0.8rem]">onEnded</span>;
      those are extensions to this contract, not part of it.
    </p>
    <DocNote>
      The output plugin is the only place that decides when audio is rendered. If playback “runs fast” or a pattern
      view is ahead of the sound, the pull pacing is the first thing to check — not the DSP.
    </DocNote>
  </Section>

  <nav class="mt-16 flex items-center justify-between gap-4 border-t border-base-300 pt-5">
    <a href={`/api/plugins/${prev.slug}`} class="font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-base-content/35 hover:text-primary">
      ← {prev.title}
    </a>
    <a href={`/api/plugins/${next.slug}`} class="text-right font-mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-base-content/50 hover:text-primary">
      {next.order} · {next.title} →
    </a>
  </nav>
</Base>
